course: dictionary
lesson: 15310
title: Sloe: a wild, sour fruit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sloe is a small, round fruit with a dark blue-black skin. It grows wild, so you may find it in hedges. Read the words around sloe to find its meaning. «We picked sloes from the hedge in October» tells you they grow outdoors, in a hedge, and are picked in autumn.
explain: «The sloes were so sour that Sam pulled a face.» Sour is the clue: a sloe tastes sharp, not sweet. «Mum made jam from the sloes.» Jam is made from fruit, so a sloe is a fruit you can cook with. Check your meaning by swapping it in: a small, dark fruit that is sour makes sense in both sentences.
explain: The same word can also name the bush. «In spring, the sloe bush is covered in white flowers.» Here the bush is the plant, not the fruit. The word that tells you is covered and flowers, which only a plant can do. When a word has two meanings, the clues in the sentence decide which one you need.
fact: A sloe is a small, round, dark blue-black fruit.
fact: Sloes are very sour when raw, so they are usually made into jam or gin rather than eaten fresh.
fact: A sloe is the fruit of the blackthorn bush, and the bush itself is sometimes called a sloe.
fact: Sloes grow wild in hedges in Britain and Ireland and ripen in autumn.
fact: Sloe gin is a drink for grown-ups, made by soaking sloes in gin.
exercise: What is a sloe? | *A small, round, dark blue-black fruit | A type of stone found in rivers | A sweet, pink sweet | A large yellow melon
exercise: «We picked sloes from the hedge in October.» Where did they grow? | In a desert | At the bottom of the sea | *In a hedge | In a shop
exercise: «The sloes were so sour that Sam pulled a face.» Find and copy one word that tells you a sloe does not taste sweet. | *sour | Sam | face | sweet
test: What plant does the sloe fruit grow on? | A bamboo plant | *The blackthorn bush | A pine tree | A rose bush
test: Why are sloes usually made into jam or gin instead of eaten raw? | Because they are sweet like sugar | Because they are white inside | Because they only grow in deserts | *Because they are very sour when raw
exam: In spring, the sloe bush is covered in flowers, so what colour are they? | *White | Red | Green | Yellow
